IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lss-dates`

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- the rules, seat-neutral. The injured person's seat
-- (lss-seat.l4) and the owner's or driver's seat (lss-seat-owner-driver.l4) ask the questions and restate none of
-- these rules. Three regulative rules (ss 35(2) and 37(3), s 38(3), s 52(1)) are run by EVALTRACE.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes. Where the text says no in its own words ("is not eligible", "is not liable", "cannot be
-- made", "may only be made by", an "if" or "while" condition that fails, a period the text fixes) the outcome begins
-- "no:"; where the text limits a grant in its own wording or is silent, it begins "not covered:" (the 2026-11-04 and
-- 2026-11-05 rulings, in substance; see NOTES.md).
--
-- The LSS Rules (made by the Governor under s 56) are not deposited: every criterion, period or limit they set is asked
-- as a fact. The Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Regulations 2014 are deposited beside this Act; they
-- prescribe no treatment, care and support need (s 4(1)(l)), no relevant determination (s 33), no matter for an expert
-- review panel (s 36(1)(e)) and no excluded cost (ss 34(10)(b)(ii), 36(6)(b)(ii), 38(11)(b)(ii)), so none of those
-- appears here as an input.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (version of 2 December 2019).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA)`

-- "the Scheme": the Scheme under this Act for the lifetime treatment, care and support of certain persons injured in
-- motor vehicle accidents (s 3(1)). "the Authority": the Lifetime Support Authority of South Australia (s 7).
-- "participant": a person accepted as a participant, lifetime or interim (s 3(1)).

-- The commencement of s 5 (and of ss 4 to 6 and Parts 3 to 6): 1 July 2014, from the legislative history ("1.7.2013
-- except ss 4-6, Pts 3-6 & Sch 1 -- 1.7.2014 (Gazette 20.6.2013 p2629)").
`the commencement of section 5` MEANS `the date` 1 7 2014

§§ `s 5 and s 6: which injuries the Act applies to`

DECLARE `Application answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to an injury from an accident on or after 1 July 2014, whoever was at fault, even if you were (s 5(1)(a), (2))`
    `yes: the accident was before 1 July 2014, but you have been accepted into the Scheme under s 6, so the Act applies (s 5(1)(b), (2))`
    `no: the Act applies to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 only where the injured person is accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1)(b))`

-- s 5(1), (2). Fork F3: s 5(1)(b)'s "where ... accepted into the Scheme under section 6" is a "where" condition, so its
-- failure answers "no" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)).
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `accepted under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`does the Act apply to the injury (s 5)` `the day of the accident` `accepted under s 6` MEANS
    IF `the commencement of section 5` `is on or before` `the day of the accident`
    THEN `yes: the Act applies to an injury from an accident on or after 1 July 2014, whoever was at fault, even if you were (s 5(1)(a), (2))`
    ELSE IF `accepted under s 6`
         THEN `yes: the accident was before 1 July 2014, but you have been accepted into the Scheme under s 6, so the Act applies (s 5(1)(b), (2))`
         ELSE `no: the Act applies to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 only where the injured person is accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1)(b))`

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a pre-commencement injury (s 6(1))` `the day of the accident` IF
    `the day of the accident` `is before` `the commencement of section 5`

-- Who makes an application (s 25(1)(b), s 6(1)(a), (3)).
DECLARE `Applicant` IS ONE OF
    `the injured person`
    `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person`
    `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident`
    `the nominal defendant`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Buy-in answer` IS ONE OF
    `not needed: the accident was on or after 1 July 2014, so the Act applies without buying in; apply under s 25 (s 5(1)(a))`
    `no: an application for a pre-commencement injury cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
    `no: s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
    `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have applied to the Authority in the manner and form it determines (s 6(1)(a))`
    `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have given the information the Authority requires (s 6(1)(b))`
    `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only if the Authority determines that it will accept you; that is the Authority's decision (s 6(1)(c))`
    `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have paid the contribution the Authority determines into the Fund (s 6(1)(d))`
    `yes: you may be accepted into the Scheme as a lifetime participant (s 6(1), (2))`

-- s 6(1), (3). Fork F4: a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person may make the s 6 application for
-- them (s 54 speaks only of participants, but says "Without limiting any other provision or law"); the nominal
-- defendant may not, because s 6(1)(a) requires "the person" to apply, and s 25 names the nominal defendant apart from
-- insurers.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant`
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave the information required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority determined to accept` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Buy-in answer`
`can the person buy in (s 6)` `the day of the accident` `the applicant` `applied` `gave the information required` `the Authority determined to accept` `paid the contribution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is a pre-commencement injury (s 6(1))` `the day of the accident`)
    THEN `not needed: the accident was on or after 1 July 2014, so the Act applies without buying in; apply under s 25 (s 5(1)(a))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the applicant`
         WHEN `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` THEN `no: an application for a pre-commencement injury cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
         WHEN `the nominal defendant` THEN `no: s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
         WHEN `someone else` THEN `no: s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
         OTHERWISE
             IF NOT `applied`
             THEN `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have applied to the Authority in the manner and form it determines (s 6(1)(a))`
             ELSE IF NOT `gave the information required`
                  THEN `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have given the information the Authority requires (s 6(1)(b))`
                  ELSE IF NOT `the Authority determined to accept`
                       THEN `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only if the Authority determines that it will accept you; that is the Authority's decision (s 6(1)(c))`
                       ELSE IF NOT `paid the contribution`
                            THEN `no: you may be accepted under s 6 only once you have paid the contribution the Authority determines into the Fund (s 6(1)(d))`
                            ELSE `yes: you may be accepted into the Scheme as a lifetime participant (s 6(1), (2))`

§§ `s 24 and s 55: eligibility`

-- The LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility, lifetime and interim (s 24(1)(e), (2)): not deposited, so asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Rules criteria` IS ONE OF
    `the injury meets the LSS Rules' criteria for lifetime participation`
    `the injury meets the LSS Rules' criteria for interim participation only`
    `the injury meets neither`

DECLARE `Eligibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: under an agreement between the Authority and a prescribed authority, no other eligibility requirement applies and you are eligible for the services the agreement contemplates (s 55(2)(a), (b))`
    `no: the Act does not apply to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 unless you are accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1))`
    `no: a person is eligible only if they suffer a bodily injury (s 24(1)(a))`
    `no: a person is eligible only if the injury was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 24(1)(b))`
    `no: a person is eligible only if the accident occurred in South Australia (s 24(1)(c))`
    `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury suffered by a participant in a road race (s 24(1)(d), (5)(a))`
    `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury that is also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014 (s 24(1)(d), (5)(b))`
    `no: a person is eligible only if the injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility (s 24(1)(e))`
    `no: a person who has been awarded damages for the future treatment, care and support needs that relate to the injury, by a final judgment or a binding settlement, is not eligible (s 24(3))`
    `yes: you are eligible to be a lifetime participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`
    `yes: you are eligible to be an interim participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`

-- s 24, read with s 5(1) and s 55(2)(a). The LSS Rules' criteria are asked; s 24(4) lifts s 24(3) for a person who has
-- applied under s 6.
GIVEN `under a s 55 agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `applied under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `suffered a bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accident occurred in South Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a participant in a road race` IS A BOOLEAN
      `also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the criteria` IS A `Rules criteria`
      `awarded damages for future needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Eligibility answer`
`is the person eligible (s 24)` `under a s 55 agreement` `the day of the accident` `applied under s 6` `suffered a bodily injury` `caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` `the accident occurred in South Australia` `a participant in a road race` `also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014` `the criteria` `awarded damages for future needs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `under a s 55 agreement`
        THEN `yes: under an agreement between the Authority and a prescribed authority, no other eligibility requirement applies and you are eligible for the services the agreement contemplates (s 55(2)(a), (b))`
        IF (`it is a pre-commencement injury (s 6(1))` `the day of the accident`) AND (NOT `applied under s 6`)
        THEN `no: the Act does not apply to an injury from an accident before 1 July 2014 unless you are accepted into the Scheme under s 6 (s 5(1))`
        IF NOT `suffered a bodily injury`
        THEN `no: a person is eligible only if they suffer a bodily injury (s 24(1)(a))`
        IF NOT `caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`
        THEN `no: a person is eligible only if the injury was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle (s 24(1)(b))`
        IF NOT `the accident occurred in South Australia`
        THEN `no: a person is eligible only if the accident occurred in South Australia (s 24(1)(c))`
        IF `a participant in a road race`
        THEN `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury suffered by a participant in a road race (s 24(1)(d), (5)(a))`
        IF `also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014`
        THEN `no: the Act's coverage is excluded for a motor vehicle injury that is also a work injury under the Return to Work Act 2014 (s 24(1)(d), (5)(b))`
        IF `the criteria` EQUALS `the injury meets neither`
        THEN `no: a person is eligible only if the injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility (s 24(1)(e))`
        IF `awarded damages for future needs` AND (NOT `applied under s 6`)
        THEN `no: a person who has been awarded damages for the future treatment, care and support needs that relate to the injury, by a final judgment or a binding settlement, is not eligible (s 24(3))`
        IF `the criteria` EQUALS `the injury meets the LSS Rules' criteria for lifetime participation`
        THEN `yes: you are eligible to be a lifetime participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are eligible to be an interim participant in the Scheme (s 24(1), (2))`

§§ `s 25 and s 6(3): who may apply`

DECLARE `Who may apply answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you may apply yourself (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
    `yes: a person with lawful authority to act on your behalf may apply (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
    `yes: an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
    `yes: the nominal defendant may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(iii), (2))`
    `no: an application may only be made by the injured person, a person with lawful authority to act for them, an insurer of a motor vehicle involved, or the nominal defendant (s 25(1)(b))`
    `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, you may apply yourself (s 6(1)(a))`
    `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, a person with lawful authority to act for you may apply on your behalf (s 6(1)(a))`
    `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, an application cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
    `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`

-- s 25(1)(b), (2); for a pre-commencement injury s 6(1)(a), (3) (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant`
GIVETH A `Who may apply answer`
`may this applicant apply (ss 25, 6)` `the day of the accident` `the applicant` MEANS
    IF `it is a pre-commencement injury (s 6(1))` `the day of the accident`
    THEN CONSIDER `the applicant`
         WHEN `the injured person` THEN `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, you may apply yourself (s 6(1)(a))`
         WHEN `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person` THEN `yes, under s 6: for an accident before 1 July 2014, a person with lawful authority to act for you may apply on your behalf (s 6(1)(a))`
         WHEN `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` THEN `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, an application cannot be made by an insurer (s 6(3))`
         OTHERWISE `no: for an accident before 1 July 2014, s 6(1)(a) requires the injured person to make the application`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the applicant`
         WHEN `the injured person` THEN `yes: you may apply yourself (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
         WHEN `a person with lawful authority to act for the injured person` THEN `yes: a person with lawful authority to act on your behalf may apply (s 25(1)(b)(i))`
         WHEN `an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident` THEN `yes: an insurer of a motor vehicle involved in the accident may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
         WHEN `the nominal defendant` THEN `yes: the nominal defendant may apply, and does not need your consent (s 25(1)(b)(iii), (2))`
         OTHERWISE `no: an application may only be made by the injured person, a person with lawful authority to act for them, an insurer of a motor vehicle involved, or the nominal defendant (s 25(1)(b))`

§§ `s 25(7), s 26(10), s 26(11): the periods the Act guarantees`

-- s 25(7): the LSS Rules "must at least permit an initial application ... within 3 years from the date of the relevant
-- motor vehicle accident". s 26(10): the LSS Rules must add any period of interim participation to the period for an
-- application to become a lifetime participant. Fork F1 for the three years; fork F2 for counting the interim days
-- (both the first and the last day counted). Fork F11: the Act sets no period for a lifetime application; s 26(10)
-- adds the interim days to the LSS Rules' period, and the 3 years plus those days is guaranteed only if that period
-- is taken to be at least the s 25(7) floor for an initial application.
GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the days of interim participation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the Act guarantees for applying (ss 25(7), 26(10))` `the day of the accident` `the days of interim participation` MEANS
    (`the day of the accident` `moved on by months` 36) `plus days` `the days of interim participation`

DECLARE `Application period answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the application is within the 3 years from the accident that the LSS Rules must at least permit (s 25(7))`
    `yes, on fork F11: the Act fixes only the 3 years for an initial application (s 25(7)) and requires the LSS Rules to add your interim participation to whatever period they set for a lifetime application (s 26(10)); taking that period to be at least the 3 years, your application is within it`
    `not covered: the application is after the period the Act guarantees; whether it may still be made depends on the LSS Rules, which may allow a longer period (s 25(6), (7))`

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the days of interim participation` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Application period answer`
`is the application within the period the Act guarantees (ss 25(7), 26(10))` `the day of the accident` `the days of interim participation` `the day of the application` MEANS
    IF `the day of the application` `is on or before` (`the day of the accident` `moved on by months` 36)
    THEN `yes: the application is within the 3 years from the accident that the LSS Rules must at least permit (s 25(7))`
    ELSE IF `the day of the application` `is on or before` (`the last day the Act guarantees for applying (ss 25(7), 26(10))` `the day of the accident` `the days of interim participation`)
         THEN `yes, on fork F11: the Act fixes only the 3 years for an initial application (s 25(7)) and requires the LSS Rules to add your interim participation to whatever period they set for a lifetime application (s 26(10)); taking that period to be at least the 3 years, your application is within it`
         ELSE `not covered: the application is after the period the Act guarantees; whether it may still be made depends on the LSS Rules, which may allow a longer period (s 25(6), (7))`

-- s 26(11): the period of interim participation is added to the 3 years under s 36 of the Limitation of Actions Act
-- 1936 (borrowed: the day the cause of action accrued is asked). Forks F1 and F2.
GIVEN `the day the cause of action accrued` IS A DATE
      `the days of interim participation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the extended limitation period (s 26(11))` `the day the cause of action accrued` `the days of interim participation` MEANS
    (`the day the cause of action accrued` `moved on by months` 36) `plus days` `the days of interim participation`

§§ `s 26: acceptance as a participant`

DECLARE `Participation kind` IS ONE OF `lifetime participation`, `interim participation`

DECLARE `Acceptance answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(2), (3)(a)), and you then remain a participant for life (s 26(5))`
    `yes: the Authority must accept you as an interim participant (s 26(2), (3)(b))`
    `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you unless it is satisfied that you are eligible; and you become a participant only if it is satisfied of that and accepts you in writing (s 26(1), (2)(a))`
    `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you until it is satisfied that the application was duly made (s 26(2)(b)); it may still accept you if it is satisfied that you are eligible (s 26(1))`

-- s 26(1) to (3). The Authority's satisfaction is a judgment left to it: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the person is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the eligibility` IS A `Participation kind`
      `the Authority is satisfied the application was duly made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Acceptance answer`
`must the Authority accept the person (s 26(1) to (3))` `the Authority is satisfied the person is eligible` `the eligibility` `the Authority is satisfied the application was duly made` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Authority is satisfied the person is eligible`
    THEN `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you unless it is satisfied that you are eligible; and you become a participant only if it is satisfied of that and accepts you in writing (s 26(1), (2)(a))`
    ELSE IF NOT `the Authority is satisfied the application was duly made`
         THEN `no: the Authority is not bound to accept you until it is satisfied that the application was duly made (s 26(2)(b)); it may still accept you if it is satisfied that you are eligible (s 26(1))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the eligibility`
              WHEN `lifetime participation` THEN `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(2), (3)(a)), and you then remain a participant for life (s 26(5))`
              WHEN `interim participation` THEN `yes: the Authority must accept you as an interim participant (s 26(2), (3)(b))`

DECLARE `Participation status` IS ONE OF
    `a lifetime participant`
    `an interim participant`
    `a person whose interim participation has ended under the LSS Rules`

DECLARE `Lifetime answer` IS ONE OF
    `already: a lifetime participant remains a participant for life (s 26(5))`
    `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(4)); you then cease to be an interim participant and remain a participant for life (s 26(9))`
    `no, not yet: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant only once it becomes satisfied, during your interim participation, that you are eligible for lifetime participation; the decision should be made at an appropriate time after your injury has stabilised (s 26(4), (6))`
    `not by s 26(4), which speaks of satisfaction during interim participation; but the end of your interim participation does not prevent your later acceptance as a lifetime participant (s 26(8))`

-- s 26(4) to (9).
GIVEN `the status` IS A `Participation status`
      `the Authority is satisfied of lifetime eligibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Lifetime answer`
`must the person be accepted as a lifetime participant (s 26(4))` `the status` `the Authority is satisfied of lifetime eligibility` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `a lifetime participant` THEN `already: a lifetime participant remains a participant for life (s 26(5))`
    WHEN `an interim participant` THEN
        IF `the Authority is satisfied of lifetime eligibility`
        THEN `yes: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant (s 26(4)); you then cease to be an interim participant and remain a participant for life (s 26(9))`
        ELSE `no, not yet: the Authority must accept you as a lifetime participant only once it becomes satisfied, during your interim participation, that you are eligible for lifetime participation; the decision should be made at an appropriate time after your injury has stabilised (s 26(4), (6))`
    WHEN `a person whose interim participation has ended under the LSS Rules` THEN `not by s 26(4), which speaks of satisfaction during interim participation; but the end of your interim participation does not prevent your later acceptance as a lifetime participant (s 26(8))`

§§ `ss 4, 27 and 28: what the Scheme pays for`

-- s 4(1): the kinds of treatment, care and support needs. Paragraph (l) (kinds prescribed by the regulations) has no
-- entry: the deposited regulations prescribe none.
DECLARE `Kind of need` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment, including pharmaceuticals`
    `dental treatment`
    `rehabilitation`
    `ambulance transportation`
    `respite care`
    `attendant care and support services`
    `aids and appliances`
    `prostheses`
    `education and vocational training`
    `home and transport modification`
    `workplace modification`
    `another kind the Authority has determined, generally or for you`
    `another kind`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of need`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a treatment, care and support need (s 4(1))` `the kind` IF
    NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `another kind`)

DECLARE `Payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the Authority pays only for expenses incurred while you are a participant in the Scheme (s 27(1))`
    `no: the Authority is not required to pay for anything provided while your participation is suspended (s 28(6))`
    `no: it is not a treatment, care and support need within s 4(1), and the Authority has not determined it to be one (s 4(1)(m))`
    `no: the LSS Rules declare it an excluded treatment, care and support need, and the Authority is not liable for it (ss 4(2), 27(3)(a))`
    `no: the Authority is not liable for a need that is not an assessed treatment, care and support need (s 27(2), (3)(b))`
    `no: the LSS Rules exclude it from the operation of s 27, and the Authority is not liable for it (s 27(3)(c))`
    `not covered: the Authority pays only the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`
    `not required: it was provided gratuitously (s 28(1)(a)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
    `not required: for a child, it falls within the ordinary costs of raising a child (s 28(1)(b), (7)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
    `not required: it must be provided by an approved provider and the provider was not approved at the time (s 28(1)(c)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
    `not required: it was provided in contravention of the LSS Rules (s 28(1)(d)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
    `yes, but only up to the limit the LSS Rules place on it (s 27(1), (4)(b))`
    `yes: the Authority is to pay the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`

-- s 3(1): "child means a person under the age of 18 years".
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a child (s 3(1))` `the age` IF `the age` LESS THAN 18

-- s 27(1) to (4), s 28(1), (4), (6), (7), s 4. The order: participation (s 27(1) "while"), suspension (s 28(6)), the
-- definition (s 4), the Authority's liability (s 27(3)), the expense (s 27(1)), the cases where payment is not required
-- (s 28(1)), and the LSS Rules' limits (s 27(4)(b)). Fork F5: a need the Authority determined under s 4(1)(m) is not
-- caught by an LSS Rules exclusion (s 4(2) "subject to subsection (1)(m)"), but s 27(3)(c) still reaches it.
GIVEN `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of need`
      `declared excluded by the LSS Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assessed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `excluded from s 27 by the LSS Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `necessary and reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provided gratuitously` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age` IS A NUMBER
      `within the ordinary costs of raising a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `must be provided by an approved provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider was approved at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the LSS Rules allow the provider to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `provided in contravention of the LSS Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `within the LSS Rules' limits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`will the Authority pay (ss 4, 27, 28)` `a participant` `suspended` `the kind` `declared excluded by the LSS Rules` `assessed by the Authority` `excluded from s 27 by the LSS Rules` `necessary and reasonable` `provided gratuitously` `the age` `within the ordinary costs of raising a child` `must be provided by an approved provider` `the provider was approved at the time` `the provider is a medical practitioner` `the LSS Rules allow the provider to act` `provided in contravention of the LSS Rules` `within the LSS Rules' limits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a participant`
        THEN `no: the Authority pays only for expenses incurred while you are a participant in the Scheme (s 27(1))`
        IF `suspended`
        THEN `no: the Authority is not required to pay for anything provided while your participation is suspended (s 28(6))`
        IF NOT (`it is a treatment, care and support need (s 4(1))` `the kind`)
        THEN `no: it is not a treatment, care and support need within s 4(1), and the Authority has not determined it to be one (s 4(1)(m))`
        IF `declared excluded by the LSS Rules` AND (NOT (`the kind` EQUALS `another kind the Authority has determined, generally or for you`))
        THEN `no: the LSS Rules declare it an excluded treatment, care and support need, and the Authority is not liable for it (ss 4(2), 27(3)(a))`
        IF NOT `assessed by the Authority`
        THEN `no: the Authority is not liable for a need that is not an assessed treatment, care and support need (s 27(2), (3)(b))`
        IF `excluded from s 27 by the LSS Rules`
        THEN `no: the LSS Rules exclude it from the operation of s 27, and the Authority is not liable for it (s 27(3)(c))`
        IF NOT `necessary and reasonable`
        THEN `not covered: the Authority pays only the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`
        IF `provided gratuitously`
        THEN `not required: it was provided gratuitously (s 28(1)(a)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
        IF (`the person is a child (s 3(1))` `the age`) AND `within the ordinary costs of raising a child`
        THEN `not required: for a child, it falls within the ordinary costs of raising a child (s 28(1)(b), (7)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
        IF `must be provided by an approved provider` AND (NOT `the provider was approved at the time`) AND (NOT `the provider is a medical practitioner`) AND (NOT `the LSS Rules allow the provider to act`)
        THEN `not required: it must be provided by an approved provider and the provider was not approved at the time (s 28(1)(c)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
        IF `provided in contravention of the LSS Rules`
        THEN `not required: it was provided in contravention of the LSS Rules (s 28(1)(d)); but the Authority may elect to pay if it considers that justified (s 28(2))`
        IF NOT `within the LSS Rules' limits`
        THEN `yes, but only up to the limit the LSS Rules place on it (s 27(1), (4)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Authority is to pay the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`

§§ `ss 39 to 41: the rate at which the Authority pays`

DECLARE `Kind of service` IS ONE OF
    `treatment at a public hospital`
    `conveying by ambulance`
    `medical treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital`
    `dental treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital`
    `rehabilitation services elsewhere than at a public hospital`
    `attendant care and support services`
    `treatment at a private hospital`
    `a service the Minister has identified for s 41 by notice in the Gazette`
    `another service`

DECLARE `Rate answer` IS ONE OF
    `at the rate the bulk billing arrangement provides (s 39(2))`
    `at the rate the Minister for Health determines by order published in the Gazette (s 40(2)(a))`
    `at the maximum rate fixed by notice in the Gazette, which is the most the Authority is liable for (ss 40(2)(b), 41(3), (5))`
    `at the rate reasonably appropriate to the treatment or service, having regard to the customary charge made in the community for it (s 40(2)(c))`
    `at most the maximum amount fixed by notice in the Gazette (s 41(3), (5))`
    `not covered: ss 40 and 41 set no rate for it; the Authority pays the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`

-- ss 39 to 41. Fork F6: a bulk billing arrangement may cover any of these expenses (s 39(1)(c) "other treatment
-- expenses" read widely); s 40 applies only where payment is not made under one. s 40(2)(b) applies "in any case in
-- which a maximum rate is fixed under section 41": ambulance is not listed in s 41(1)(a) to (d), but the Minister may
-- bring it within s 41 by Gazette notice (s 41(1)(e)), so its rate turns on whether a maximum has been fixed. Treatment
-- at a private hospital is "medical or dental treatment" within s 40(1)(c), so s 40(2)(b) or (c) applies to it.
GIVEN `the service` IS A `Kind of service`
      `paid under a bulk billing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a maximum fee has been fixed for it under s 41` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Rate answer`
`at what rate does the Authority pay (ss 39 to 41)` `the service` `paid under a bulk billing arrangement` `a maximum fee has been fixed for it under s 41` MEANS
    IF `paid under a bulk billing arrangement`
    THEN `at the rate the bulk billing arrangement provides (s 39(2))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the service`
         WHEN `treatment at a public hospital` THEN `at the rate the Minister for Health determines by order published in the Gazette (s 40(2)(a))`
         WHEN `conveying by ambulance` THEN `s 40 rate`
         WHEN `medical treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital` THEN `s 40 rate`
         WHEN `dental treatment elsewhere than at a public hospital` THEN `s 40 rate`
         WHEN `rehabilitation services elsewhere than at a public hospital` THEN `s 40 rate`
         WHEN `treatment at a private hospital` THEN `s 40 rate`
         WHEN `another service` THEN `not covered: ss 40 and 41 set no rate for it; the Authority pays the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`
         OTHERWISE
             IF `a maximum fee has been fixed for it under s 41`
             THEN `at most the maximum amount fixed by notice in the Gazette (s 41(3), (5))`
             ELSE `not covered: ss 40 and 41 set no rate for it; the Authority pays the necessary and reasonable expenses (s 27(1))`
    WHERE
        `s 40 rate` MEANS
            IF `a maximum fee has been fixed for it under s 41`
            THEN `at the maximum rate fixed by notice in the Gazette, which is the most the Authority is liable for (ss 40(2)(b), 41(3), (5))`
            ELSE `at the rate reasonably appropriate to the treatment or service, having regard to the customary charge made in the community for it (s 40(2)(c))`

§§ `ss 30 to 32: the needs assessment`

DECLARE `Cooperation answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you must comply with a reasonable request made in connection with the assessment of your needs, including a request to undergo an examination (s 31); if the LSS Rules so provide, failing to comply with a requirement for the assessment can lead to the suspension of your participation (s 32(2)(e))`
    `not covered: s 31 binds participants in the Scheme`
    `not covered: s 31 applies to requests by the Authority or an assessor in connection with an assessment of your treatment, care and support needs`
    `not covered: s 31 requires you to comply only with a reasonable request`

-- s 31, s 32(2)(e). Whether a request is reasonable is a judgment: asked as a fact.
GIVEN `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made by the Authority or an assessor for the needs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Cooperation answer`
`must the participant comply with the request (s 31)` `a participant` `made by the Authority or an assessor for the needs assessment` `the request is reasonable` MEANS
    IF NOT `a participant`
    THEN `not covered: s 31 binds participants in the Scheme`
    ELSE IF NOT `made by the Authority or an assessor for the needs assessment`
         THEN `not covered: s 31 applies to requests by the Authority or an assessor in connection with an assessment of your treatment, care and support needs`
         ELSE IF NOT `the request is reasonable`
              THEN `not covered: s 31 requires you to comply only with a reasonable request`
              ELSE `yes: you must comply with a reasonable request made in connection with the assessment of your needs, including a request to undergo an examination (s 31); if the LSS Rules so provide, failing to comply with a requirement for the assessment can lead to the suspension of your participation (s 32(2)(e))`

§§ `Part 5: disputes and reviews`

-- The decisions Part 5 deals with. The first five are "threshold determinations" (s 33(1)); the suspension is the second
-- kind of "relevant determination"; the next four are s 36(1)(a) to (d) disputes; then the s 38 assessment.
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    `whether I suffered a bodily injury`
    `whether the incident was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`
    `whether the accident occurred in South Australia`
    `whether the Act's coverage is excluded because of a road race or a work injury`
    `whether my application was made within the period the LSS Rules specify`
    `a determination that suspends my participation`
    `whether my injury resulted from the accident or from some other condition, event or factor`
    `whether my injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility`
    `how two or more of my injuries are related`
    `whether my injury is within or excluded from the coverage of the Act under the LSS Rules`
    `the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `Review route answer` IS ONE OF
    `a review officer first: you may apply to have the dispute reviewed by a review officer (s 34(1)); then, as a party, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of the review officer's determination (s 35)`
    `an expert review panel: the dispute may be referred to a panel by notice given to the Authority by you or on your behalf (s 36(1), (2)(b)(i)); if the panel determines that you are ineligible or do not qualify, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of its determination (s 37)`
    `an expert review panel review of the assessment: apply within 28 days after you are given notice of the assessment, unless the LSS Rules allow more time; the panel's decision is final and binding for the purposes of the Act, though not against judicial review (s 38)`
    `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`
    `not covered: Part 5 provides no review of this decision; the Authority's code of conduct must include a process for complaints about how it exercised a function or power (s 23(2)(a))`

-- ss 33 to 38. The person to whom an application relates is an interested party in a threshold determination
-- (s 33(2)(a)(i)) and the person to whom any other relevant determination relates is one too (s 33(2)(b)).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision`
      `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Review route answer`
`which review is open (Part 5)` `the decision` `a participant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `whether I suffered a bodily injury` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `whether the incident was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `whether the accident occurred in South Australia` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `whether the Act's coverage is excluded because of a road race or a work injury` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `whether my application was made within the period the LSS Rules specify` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `a determination that suspends my participation` THEN `review officer route`
    WHEN `whether my injury resulted from the accident or from some other condition, event or factor` THEN `panel route`
    WHEN `whether my injury satisfies the LSS Rules' criteria for eligibility` THEN `panel route`
    WHEN `how two or more of my injuries are related` THEN `panel route`
    WHEN `whether my injury is within or excluded from the coverage of the Act under the LSS Rules` THEN `panel route`
    WHEN `the assessment of my treatment, care and support needs` THEN
        IF `a participant`
        THEN `an expert review panel review of the assessment: apply within 28 days after you are given notice of the assessment, unless the LSS Rules allow more time; the panel's decision is final and binding for the purposes of the Act, though not against judicial review (s 38)`
        ELSE `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`
    WHEN `another decision` THEN `not covered: Part 5 provides no review of this decision; the Authority's code of conduct must include a process for complaints about how it exercised a function or power (s 23(2)(a))`
    WHERE
        `review officer route` MEANS `a review officer first: you may apply to have the dispute reviewed by a review officer (s 34(1)); then, as a party, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of the review officer's determination (s 35)`
        `panel route` MEANS `an expert review panel: the dispute may be referred to a panel by notice given to the Authority by you or on your behalf (s 36(1), (2)(b)(i)); if the panel determines that you are ineligible or do not qualify, you may apply to the Tribunal within 28 days of its determination (s 37)`

DECLARE `Forum` IS ONE OF
    `a review officer (s 34)`
    `an expert review panel on an eligibility dispute (s 36)`
    `an expert review panel reviewing my needs assessment (s 38)`
    `the Tribunal (ss 35, 37)`

DECLARE `Cost` IS ONE OF
    `my travel and accommodation to attend`
    `the travel and accommodation of a carer who accompanies and supports me`
    `the cost of being represented`
    `another cost of the proceedings`

DECLARE `Costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including your necessary travel and accommodation costs in attending (ss 34(9), (10)(a), 36(5), (6)(a), 38(10), (11)(a))`
    `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including the necessary travel and accommodation costs of a carer (who may be a parent) who accompanies and supports you (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
    `yes: the costs of the proceedings are payable by the Authority (ss 34(9), 36(5), 38(10))`
    `no: the costs the Authority pays do not include any costs of being represented (ss 34(10)(b)(i), 36(6)(b)(i), 38(11)(b)(i))`
    `not covered: travel and accommodation costs are included only so far as they are necessary (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
    `not covered: the Act says nothing of costs before the Tribunal`

-- ss 34(9), (10), 36(5), (6), 38(10), (11). The deposited regulations exclude no costs.
GIVEN `the forum` IS A `Forum`
      `the cost` IS A `Cost`
      `the cost is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Costs answer`
`does the Authority pay this cost (ss 34, 36, 38)` `the forum` `the cost` `the cost is necessary` MEANS
    IF `the forum` EQUALS `the Tribunal (ss 35, 37)`
    THEN `not covered: the Act says nothing of costs before the Tribunal`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the cost`
         WHEN `the cost of being represented` THEN `no: the costs the Authority pays do not include any costs of being represented (ss 34(10)(b)(i), 36(6)(b)(i), 38(11)(b)(i))`
         WHEN `another cost of the proceedings` THEN `yes: the costs of the proceedings are payable by the Authority (ss 34(9), 36(5), 38(10))`
         WHEN `my travel and accommodation to attend` THEN
             IF `the cost is necessary`
             THEN `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including your necessary travel and accommodation costs in attending (ss 34(9), (10)(a), 36(5), (6)(a), 38(10), (11)(a))`
             ELSE `not covered: travel and accommodation costs are included only so far as they are necessary (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
         WHEN `the travel and accommodation of a carer who accompanies and supports me` THEN
             IF `the cost is necessary`
             THEN `yes: the Authority pays the costs of the proceedings, including the necessary travel and accommodation costs of a carer (who may be a parent) who accompanies and supports you (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`
             ELSE `not covered: travel and accommodation costs are included only so far as they are necessary (ss 34(10)(a), 36(6)(a), 38(11)(a))`

§§ `The deadlines, as regulative rules (ss 35(2), 37(3), 38(3), 52(1))`

-- Each rule counts on the day-number timeline (DATE_SERIAL): the trace starts at day 0 and WITHIN is the day number of
-- the last day, so an act on or before the last day fulfils the rule and an act after it breaches.

DECLARE `Scheme party` IS ONE OF `the person injured`

DECLARE `Scheme step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Tribunal for review`
    `apply for review of the needs assessment`
    `give the Authority notice of the proposed absence`

GIVEN `the last day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme step`
`ss 35(2), 37(3) -- an application to the Tribunal must be made within 28 days of the determination` `the last day number` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person injured`
    MUST   `apply to the Tribunal for review`
    WITHIN `the last day number`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person injured` BECAUSE "ss 35(2), 37(3): the application for review was not made within 28 days of the date of the determination"

GIVEN `the last day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme step`
`s 38(3) -- an application for review of the assessment must be made within 28 days after notice` `the last day number` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person injured`
    MUST   `apply for review of the needs assessment`
    WITHIN `the last day number`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person injured` BECAUSE "s 38(3): the application was not made within 28 days after notice of the assessment"

GIVEN `the last day number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme step`
`s 52(1) -- notice of the absence must be given at least 28 days before leaving Australia` `the last day number` MEANS
    PARTY  `the person injured`
    MUST   `give the Authority notice of the proposed absence`
    WITHIN `the last day number`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the person injured` BECAUSE "s 52(1): notice of the proposed absence was not given at least 28 days before leaving Australia"

DECLARE `Timing` IS ONE OF `in time`, `out of time`, `still in time`

-- Runs a rule: where the step was taken, FULFILLED means in time and anything else late; where it was not, whether
-- taking it today would still be in time. On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED only.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO DEONTIC `Scheme party` `Scheme step`
      `the step` IS A `Scheme step`
      `the last day` IS A DATE
      `taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day taken` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Timing`
`the timing of` `the rule` `the step` `the last day` `taken` `the day taken` `today` MEANS
    IF `taken`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the rule` (DATE_SERIAL `the last day`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person injured` `the step` (DATE_SERIAL `the day taken`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time`
         OTHERWISE `out of time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the rule` (DATE_SERIAL `the last day`)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person injured` `the step` (DATE_SERIAL `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time`
         OTHERWISE `out of time`

-- ss 35(2), 37(3): "within 28 days of the date of the determination" (fork F2: the last day is that date plus 28).
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to the Tribunal (ss 35(2), 37(3))` `the day of the determination` MEANS
    `the day of the determination` `plus days` 28

DECLARE `Tribunal route` IS ONE OF
    `review of a review officer's determination (s 35)`
    `review of an expert review panel's determination that I am ineligible or do not qualify (s 37)`

DECLARE `Tribunal answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 35 lets a party to the dispute apply to the Tribunal`
    `in time: the application was made within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
    `still in time: you may apply to the Tribunal, within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
    `no: an application for review must be made within 28 days of the date of the determination, and that time has passed (ss 35(2), 37(3))`

GIVEN `the route` IS A `Tribunal route`
      `a party to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tribunal answer`
`may the person apply to the Tribunal (ss 35, 37)` `the route` `a party to the dispute` `the day of the determination` `applied` `the day applied` `today` MEANS
    IF (`the route` EQUALS `review of a review officer's determination (s 35)`) AND (NOT `a party to the dispute`)
    THEN `not covered: s 35 lets a party to the dispute apply to the Tribunal`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the timing of` `ss 35(2), 37(3) -- an application to the Tribunal must be made within 28 days of the determination` `apply to the Tribunal for review` (`the last day to apply to the Tribunal (ss 35(2), 37(3))` `the day of the determination`) `applied` `the day applied` `today`
         WHEN `in time` THEN `in time: the application was made within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
         WHEN `still in time` THEN `still in time: you may apply to the Tribunal, within 28 days of the date of the determination (ss 35(2), 37(3))`
         WHEN `out of time` THEN `no: an application for review must be made within 28 days of the date of the determination, and that time has passed (ss 35(2), 37(3))`

-- s 38(3): "within 28 days after the participant is given notice of the assessment" (fork F2).
GIVEN `the day of notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for review of the assessment (s 38(3))` `the day of notice` MEANS
    `the day of notice` `plus days` 28

DECLARE `Assessment review answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`
    `in time: the application was made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
    `still in time: you may apply, within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
    `the LSS Rules' extension governs: the 28 days do not apply where an extension of time is allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`
    `no: the application must be made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment, that time has passed, and no extension has been allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`

GIVEN `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of notice` IS A DATE
      `an extension has been allowed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Assessment review answer`
`may the participant apply for review of the assessment (s 38)` `a participant` `the day of notice` `an extension has been allowed` `applied` `the day applied` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `a participant`
    THEN `not covered: s 38 lets a participant in the Scheme apply for review of an assessment`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the timing of` `s 38(3) -- an application for review of the assessment must be made within 28 days after notice` `apply for review of the needs assessment` (`the last day to apply for review of the assessment (s 38(3))` `the day of notice`) `applied` `the day applied` `today`
         WHEN `in time` THEN `in time: the application was made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
         WHEN `still in time` THEN `still in time: you may apply, within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment (s 38(3))`
         WHEN `out of time` THEN
             IF `an extension has been allowed`
             THEN `the LSS Rules' extension governs: the 28 days do not apply where an extension of time is allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`
             ELSE `no: the application must be made within 28 days after you were given notice of the assessment, that time has passed, and no extension has been allowed under the LSS Rules (s 38(3))`

§§ `s 52: absence from Australia`

-- s 52(1): "at least 28 days before leaving Australia" (fork F2: the last day is the day of leaving less 28).
GIVEN `the day of leaving` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to give notice of the absence (s 52(1))` `the day of leaving` MEANS
    `the day of leaving` `plus days` (0 MINUS 28)

DECLARE `Absence answer` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 52 binds participants in the Scheme`
    `the Authority has waived or reduced the period: the 28 days do not apply to you as they stand (s 52(2)(a))`
    `in time: you gave notice at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may still suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
    `still in time: give the Authority notice, in accordance with the LSS Rules, at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
    `no: notice must be given at least 28 days before leaving Australia (s 52(1)); the Authority may waive or reduce that period (s 52(2)(a)), and may suspend your participation while you are absent whether or not notice was given (s 52(2)(b))`

GIVEN `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of leaving` IS A DATE
      `the Authority waived or reduced the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of notice` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Absence answer`
`has the participant given notice of the absence in time (s 52)` `a participant` `the day of leaving` `the Authority waived or reduced the period` `gave notice` `the day of notice` `today` MEANS
    IF NOT `a participant`
    THEN `not covered: s 52 binds participants in the Scheme`
    ELSE IF `the Authority waived or reduced the period`
         THEN `the Authority has waived or reduced the period: the 28 days do not apply to you as they stand (s 52(2)(a))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the timing of` `s 52(1) -- notice of the absence must be given at least 28 days before leaving Australia` `give the Authority notice of the proposed absence` (`the last day to give notice of the absence (s 52(1))` `the day of leaving`) `gave notice` `the day of notice` `today`
              WHEN `in time` THEN `in time: you gave notice at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may still suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
              WHEN `still in time` THEN `still in time: give the Authority notice, in accordance with the LSS Rules, at least 28 days before leaving (s 52(1)); the Authority may suspend your participation while you are absent (s 52(2)(b))`
              WHEN `out of time` THEN `no: notice must be given at least 28 days before leaving Australia (s 52(1)); the Authority may waive or reduce that period (s 52(2)(a)), and may suspend your participation while you are absent whether or not notice was given (s 52(2)(b))`

§§ `ss 34(6), 51: offences`

DECLARE `Conduct` IS ONE OF
    `giving information to the Authority or another person acting under the Act`
    `leaving information out of what I give to a person acting under the Act`
    `failing to appear, answer questions or produce material when a review officer requires it`
    `something else`

-- s 51 (maximum penalty $10 000) and s 34(6) (maximum penalty $5 000). Knowledge and materiality are asked as facts;
-- whether an excuse is reasonable is a judgment for the court, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct`
      `I knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty (ss 34(6), 51)` `the conduct` `I knew it was false or misleading` `false or misleading in a material particular` `a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `giving information to the Authority or another person acting under the Act` THEN `s 51 penalty`
    WHEN `leaving information out of what I give to a person acting under the Act` THEN `s 51 penalty`
    WHEN `failing to appear, answer questions or produce material when a review officer requires it` THEN
        IF `a reasonable excuse` THEN 0 ELSE 5000
    WHEN `something else` THEN 0
    WHERE
        `s 51 penalty` MEANS
            IF `I knew it was false or misleading` AND `false or misleading in a material particular`
            THEN 10000
            ELSE 0

§§ `ss 45 and 46: recovery by the Authority from an owner, a driver or another person at fault`

DECLARE `Role` IS ONE OF
    `the owner of the vehicle, and someone else was driving`
    `the driver of the vehicle, and not its owner`
    `the owner and the driver of the vehicle`
    `another person partly at fault, not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle`

DECLARE `Recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the Authority recovers under s 45 only the costs of the injury of a participant in the Scheme (s 45(1))`
    `no: the Authority may not recover where the participant paid an amount to the Authority under s 6 for those injuries (s 45(10))`
    `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the share of the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities that corresponds to your share in the responsibility for the injury (s 45(3), (4))`
    `not covered: s 45(3) reaches a person, other than an owner or driver, who was partly at fault for the injury`
    `no: s 45(1) applies only if the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in its use or operation (s 45(1)(a))`
    `no: s 45(1) applies only if the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires at the time of the accident (s 45(1)(b))`
    `no: the Authority may not recover from the owner or driver of a vehicle that was not required to be registered, was exempt from registration, or was not required to be insured (s 45(8))`
    `no: you have a sufficient defence as owner if you establish to the court's satisfaction that someone else was driving without your authority (s 45(6))`
    `no: you have a sufficient defence as driver if you establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed you had it) and reasonably believed the vehicle was insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires (s 45(7))`
    `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the injury, reduced for the participant's contributory negligence; where the owner and someone else as driver are both liable, jointly or either of you severally (s 45(1), (2), (4), (5))`

-- s 45. "Fault", "contributory negligence" and "share in the responsibility" are borrowed and asked; the defences in
-- s 45(6) and (7) are for the person to establish "to the satisfaction of the court", asked as facts. Fork F7: s 45(3)
-- is read as standing on its own words, not limited to an uninsured vehicle (s 45(1)(b)). Fork F12: a person who
-- was both owner and driver is treated as owner (s 45(5)) and has neither the s 45(6) nor the s 45(7) defence.
GIVEN `the role` IS A `Role`
      `the injured person is a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the participant bought in under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vehicle was not required to be registered or insured, or was exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was partly at fault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner's defence is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the driver's defence is established` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`can the Authority recover from this person (s 45)` `the role` `the injured person is a participant` `the participant bought in under s 6` `caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 requires` `the vehicle was not required to be registered or insured, or was exempt` `I was partly at fault` `the owner's defence is established` `the driver's defence is established` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the injured person is a participant`
        THEN `no: the Authority recovers under s 45 only the costs of the injury of a participant in the Scheme (s 45(1))`
        IF `the participant bought in under s 6`
        THEN `no: the Authority may not recover where the participant paid an amount to the Authority under s 6 for those injuries (s 45(10))`
        IF `the role` EQUALS `another person partly at fault, not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle`
        THEN IF `I was partly at fault`
             THEN `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the share of the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities that corresponds to your share in the responsibility for the injury (s 45(3), (4))`
             ELSE `not covered: s 45(3) reaches a person, other than an owner or driver, who was partly at fault for the injury`
        IF NOT `caused by the fault of the owner or driver`
        THEN `no: s 45(1) applies only if the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in its use or operation (s 45(1)(a))`
        IF NOT `the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 requires`
        THEN `no: s 45(1) applies only if the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires at the time of the accident (s 45(1)(b))`
        IF `the vehicle was not required to be registered or insured, or was exempt`
        THEN `no: the Authority may not recover from the owner or driver of a vehicle that was not required to be registered, was exempt from registration, or was not required to be insured (s 45(8))`
        IF (`the role` EQUALS `the owner of the vehicle, and someone else was driving`) AND `the owner's defence is established`
        THEN `no: you have a sufficient defence as owner if you establish to the court's satisfaction that someone else was driving without your authority (s 45(6))`
        IF (`the role` EQUALS `the driver of the vehicle, and not its owner`) AND `the driver's defence is established`
        THEN `no: you have a sufficient defence as driver if you establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed you had it) and reasonably believed the vehicle was insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires (s 45(7))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the injury, reduced for the participant's contributory negligence; where the owner and someone else as driver are both liable, jointly or either of you severally (s 45(1), (2), (4), (5))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Recovery answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recovery lies in full, less contributory negligence` `the answer` IF
    `the answer` EQUALS `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the injury, reduced for the participant's contributory negligence; where the owner and someone else as driver are both liable, jointly or either of you severally (s 45(1), (2), (4), (5))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Recovery answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `recovery lies for a share` `the answer` IF
    `the answer` EQUALS `yes: the Authority may recover from you as a debt the share of the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities that corresponds to your share in the responsibility for the injury (s 45(3), (4))`

-- s 45(4): the present value is the sum of what the Authority has already paid under Part 4 for the injury and the
-- present value of what it estimates it will pay in future (the Authority's certificate is evidence of it, s 45(9)).
GIVEN `already paid` IS A NUMBER, `present value of future payments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the present value of the Authority's liabilities (s 45(4))` `already paid` `present value of future payments` MEANS
    `already paid` PLUS `present value of future payments`

-- s 45(1), (2), (3), (4). Shares are percentages (0 to 100). Nothing is recoverable where the s 45 answer is no.
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Recovery answer`
      `already paid` IS A NUMBER
      `present value of future payments` IS A NUMBER
      `the participant's share in the responsibility` IS A NUMBER
      `my share in the responsibility` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Authority can recover (s 45)` `the answer` `already paid` `present value of future payments` `the participant's share in the responsibility` `my share in the responsibility` MEANS
    IF `recovery lies in full, less contributory negligence` `the answer`
    THEN `the present value` TIMES ((100 MINUS `the participant's share in the responsibility`) DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE IF `recovery lies for a share` `the answer`
         THEN `the present value` TIMES (`my share in the responsibility` DIVIDED BY 100)
         ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the present value` MEANS `the present value of the Authority's liabilities (s 45(4))` `already paid` `present value of future payments`

DECLARE `Default recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Authority may exercise against you the same right of recovery the insurer or nominal defendant has under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959, for the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the participant (s 46(1), (2), (4))`
    `no: s 46 applies only if an approved insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against you under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (s 46(1)(a))`
    `no: s 46 applies only if the injured person becomes a participant in the Scheme (s 46(1)(b))`

-- s 46. The right of recovery under the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 ss 116, 124A is borrowed and asked.
GIVEN `an insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the injured person became a participant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Default recovery answer`
`can the Authority use the right of recovery (s 46)` `an insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against me` `the injured person became a participant` MEANS
    IF NOT `an insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against me`
    THEN `no: s 46 applies only if an approved insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against you under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 (s 46(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF NOT `the injured person became a participant`
         THEN `no: s 46 applies only if the injured person becomes a participant in the Scheme (s 46(1)(b))`
         ELSE `yes: the Authority may exercise against you the same right of recovery the insurer or nominal defendant has under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959, for the present value of its treatment, care and support liabilities for the participant (s 46(1), (2), (4))`

§§ `s 49 and Schedule 1 cl 6(7): assessors, review officers and panels`

DECLARE `Immunity answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: they are not personally liable for what they did or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act; the liability attaches instead to the Crown (s 49(1), (2))`
    `not covered: s 49 protects only what was done or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act`

-- s 49. Good faith is a fact for the court: asked.
GIVEN `in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Immunity answer`
`can the officer be sued personally (s 49)` `in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act` `in good faith` MEANS
    IF `in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act` AND `in good faith`
    THEN `no: they are not personally liable for what they did or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act; the liability attaches instead to the Crown (s 49(1), (2))`
    ELSE `not covered: s 49 protects only what was done or omitted in good faith in performing a function or exercising a power under the Act`

DECLARE `Panel information answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in proceedings before a court or the Tribunal (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(a))`
    `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in other proceedings because you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(b))`
    `no: information given to an expert review panel cannot be used in subsequent proceedings unless they are before a court or the Tribunal, or you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7))`

-- Schedule 1 cl 6(7).
GIVEN `before a court or the Tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Panel information answer`
`can panel information be used in later proceedings (Sch 1 cl 6(7))` `before a court or the Tribunal` `the person consents` MEANS
    IF `before a court or the Tribunal`
    THEN `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in proceedings before a court or the Tribunal (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(a))`
    ELSE IF `the person consents`
         THEN `yes: information given to an expert review panel may be used in other proceedings because you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7)(b))`
         ELSE `no: information given to an expert review panel cannot be used in subsequent proceedings unless they are before a court or the Tribunal, or you consent (Schedule 1 cl 6(7))`
